# ─── Misc ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Kept on every branch even where the directory does not exist: these rules are
# what stop 54M of PNG mocks from being swept in by a `git add -A`.
prototypes/
*.log
logs/
tmp/
temp/
.cache/
.parcel-cache/
.turbo/
.vercel/
.netlify/
*.tsbuildinfo

# sssf runtime
adws/adw_data/sessions/
# Unanchored: a trace db is never committed, wherever it turns up. Two empty
# ones had been tracked — adws/sssf.db and templates/adws/sssf.db, the second
# of which would have stamped a fake trace db into every target repo.
sssf.db*

# Claude Skills
.claude/skills/*
# ...except the sssf factory. Its template tree IS what the factory ships from
# and is deliberately tracked (236 files). Ignoring it does not untrack those,
# so nothing looks wrong — but every NEW runtime file under it becomes invisible
# to `git add`, which is exactly the silent-loss shape CLAUDE.md records.
!.claude/skills/sssf/

# demo app runtime (example branch)
apps/inkwell/inkwell.db*
scratchpad/*

*.mov
.agent_memory.json
.agent_memory/

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Agent-harness state must never reach the installable tree
.omc/
.omp/
.lex/
